            <ArticleTitle>Bladder leiomyoma: a rare cause of pelvic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>896</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Leiomyoma of the bladder is an unusual cause of persistent bladder or pelvic pain. Traditional modalities may enable the clinical to suspect the diagnosis, which should be confirmed by transurethral biopsy. Except in rare circumstances, the treatment of choice is a suprapubic abdominal approach for removal of the bladder tumor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
